From: openHC <noreply@openhc>
Subject: [PATCH] Page: honour OHC_DISPLAY_THEME as the page color scheme

The on-panel display service (S95ohc-display) exports OHC_DISPLAY_THEME —
light|dark|auto, set from the web UI's day/night control — into the webview's
environment, which the WPE WebProcess inherits.

WPE on LinuxFB has no desktop/toolkit dark-mode signal to follow (the way
WebKitGTK follows the GTK theme), so without this the engine always reports a
light preference and `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` never matches on the
panel. Honour the env in Page::useDarkAppearance() — the single lever the media
query, the `color-scheme` CSS property and native form-control rendering all
read — so the whole page responds like OS dark mode, for any site, not just one
that reads a query parameter. "auto" or unset falls through to WebKit's normal
behaviour, so this is inert off the panel.

Read once (kiosk env is fixed for the life of the process; a theme change
restarts the view). This is a local openHC kiosk knob, not a public API; a
proper WebKitSettings/WebKitWebView property wired to setUseDarkAppearance-
Override would be the upstream form.

--- a/Source/WebCore/page/Page.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/page/Page.cpp
@@ -204,6 +204,7 @@
 #include "WorkerOrWorkletScriptController.h"
 #include <JavaScriptCore/VM.h>
 #include <ranges>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <wtf/FileSystem.h>
 #include <wtf/RefCountedLeakCounter.h>
 #include <wtf/StdLibExtras.h>
@@ -4297,6 +4298,25 @@
 bool Page::useDarkAppearance() const
 {
 #if ENABLE(DARK_MODE_CSS)
+    // openHC: the on-panel display service exports OHC_DISPLAY_THEME (light|dark|
+    // auto) from the web UI's day/night setting. WPE on LinuxFB has no desktop
+    // dark-mode signal to follow, so honour that env here as the page's color
+    // scheme: prefers-color-scheme, the color-scheme CSS property and native form
+    // controls then all respond like OS dark mode, for any page. Read once; "auto"
+    // or unset falls through to WebKit's normal behaviour. Local openHC kiosk
+    // knob, not an upstream API.
+    static const int ohcColorScheme = [] {
+        if (const char* theme = getenv("OHC_DISPLAY_THEME")) {
+            if (theme[0] == 'd')
+                return 1;
+            if (theme[0] == 'l')
+                return 0;
+        }
+        return -1;
+    }();
+    if (ohcColorScheme >= 0)
+        return ohcColorScheme == 1;
+
     RefPtr localMainFrame = this->localMainFrame();

     // FIXME: If this page is being printed, this function should return false.
